1
00:00:01,164 --> 00:00:05,164
[bright music]

2
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:43,916
Hi, how can I help you?

3
00:00:43,958 --> 00:00:45,041
Marlboros.

4
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:47,041
Come again?

5
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,583
Can I get some Marlboros? Are you deaf?

6
00:00:51,291 --> 00:00:51,916
Uh…

7
00:00:52,166 --> 00:00:53,083
One pack?

8
00:00:53,791 --> 00:00:55,583
No, just a loosie.

9
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:07,375
Are you fucking kidding me, right now?

10
00:01:08,291 --> 00:01:10,416
You’re really just gonna give me a loosie?

11
00:01:10,458 --> 00:01:12,958
Sorry, I thought ‘loosie’ meant stick.

12
00:01:13,791 --> 00:01:16,374
In the Philippines, we actually
sell cigarettes by the stick.

13
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:18,833
I don't care wherever the hell you're from.

14
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:22,166
If you don’t know anything about
this country, why even come here?

15
00:01:25,052 --> 00:01:29,052
[suspenseful music]

16
00:01:29,291 --> 00:01:31,583
I don't like that. It's opened.

17
00:01:31,625 --> 00:01:33,541
Give me a new one.

18
00:01:38,791 --> 00:01:40,333
Will that be cash or card?

19
00:01:40,375 --> 00:01:41,833
Cash!

20
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:43,666
Idiot.

21
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:48,333
You can remove it.

22
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:52,708
Fucking Asian.

23
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,458
Excuse me, what did you just call me?

24
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:56,291
I said fucking Asian.

25
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:57,666
Do you have a problem with that?

26
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:58,541
Yeah.

27
00:01:58,583 --> 00:01:59,833
Maybe I do!

28
00:01:59,875 --> 00:02:02,083
Then why don't you go back to China?

29
00:02:02,125 --> 00:02:03,833
You don't belong here!

30
00:02:04,083 --> 00:02:06,625
Maybe 'cause I'm not from China.

31
00:02:06,791 --> 00:02:08,208
I'm from the Philippines.

32
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:12,083
What did you say?

33
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:13,624
I said I'm not from China.

34
00:02:13,666 --> 00:02:15,458
I'm from the Philippines!

35
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,583
It's the same fucking
difference, you idiot!

36
00:02:23,859 --> 00:02:27,859
[suspenseful music]

37
00:02:29,875 --> 00:02:31,166
I'm back.

38
00:02:33,875 --> 00:02:34,750
Andre?

39
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:41,708
Hello?

40
00:02:44,958 --> 00:02:46,416
Where are you?

41
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,125
What happened to your face?

42
00:03:01,416 --> 00:03:02,375
Nothing.

43
00:03:02,625 --> 00:03:03,791
Turn around.

44
00:03:04,541 --> 00:03:05,708
I'm busy.

45
00:03:05,958 --> 00:03:07,125
Look at me.

46
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,666
I said I'm busy.

47
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:14,666
What happened to you?

48
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:21,166
You can’t fight with robbers here, okay?

49
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:24,166
They carry guns. You could’ve gotten shot.

50
00:03:26,416 --> 00:03:28,166
It wasn’t a robber.

51
00:03:31,625 --> 00:03:33,583
Who did this to you?

52
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:36,958
Did...

53
00:03:37,333 --> 00:03:40,208
Did you get into a fight with a customer?

54
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:46,125
I knew it.

55
00:03:46,708 --> 00:03:48,874
I knew I couldn’t trust you with the store!

56
00:03:48,916 --> 00:03:53,291
You... you're arrogant and
impulsive and irresponsible!

57
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:55,500
What did you do to the customer?

58
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:05,166
I told him he should know the difference
between the Philippines and China.

59
00:04:06,291 --> 00:04:07,000
What?

60
00:04:25,916 --> 00:04:29,916
[piano music]

61
00:04:31,199 --> 00:04:34,835
[applause]

62
00:04:34,875 --> 00:04:36,166
Oh, wow!

63
00:04:37,375 --> 00:04:38,708
Uh, thank you.

64
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:42,500
Thank you to the Hollywood Prestige
International Short Film Festival.

65
00:04:42,625 --> 00:04:46,541
Um, shoutout to everyone – staff
and organizers who put this together.

66
00:04:46,583 --> 00:04:51,833
And, of course, this one goes out to
all the aspiring filmmakers and artists.

67
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,833
Anyone whose voice has never been heard,

68
00:04:53,875 --> 00:04:55,666
anyone who feels unrecognized out there,

69
00:04:55,708 --> 00:04:57,916
this one’s for you. And...

70
00:04:58,208 --> 00:04:59,333
Oh my God!

71
00:04:59,375 --> 00:05:02,374
Just thank you to Hollywood for
opening doors for more people like us.

72
00:05:02,416 --> 00:05:03,791
Thank you, thank you.

73
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:05,666
More love. Woah!

74
00:05:08,357 --> 00:05:12,357
[applause]

75
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:16,958
Hey,

76
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,999
you're the filmmaker
from the Philippines, right?

77
00:05:19,041 --> 00:05:19,958
Oh, uh...

78
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,791
I'm Ethan Bloom, with Hollywood Prestige.

79
00:05:25,583 --> 00:05:27,041
I’m so sorry. I didn’t…

80
00:05:27,083 --> 00:05:29,708
No worries. I just wanna
come over and congratulate you.

81
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:30,958
I saw your short.

82
00:05:31,083 --> 00:05:33,125
I was really blown away.
That was great work.

83
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,333
Oh, wow. Uh...

84
00:05:35,375 --> 00:05:38,208
Thank you. Coming from a Hollywood
Producer like yourself, that means a lot.

85
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:39,583
Don't mention it.

86
00:05:39,625 --> 00:05:40,958
So who are you here with?

87
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,374
Just by myself.

88
00:05:42,416 --> 00:05:45,583
Hm… And how long are you
planning to stay here in LA?

89
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,750
Just a couple of days.

90
00:05:47,875 --> 00:05:49,125
That’s too bad.

91
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:50,916
Why?

92
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:54,291
Well, I’m working on a special project and…

93
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:56,791
I’d like you to be a part of it.

94
00:05:57,708 --> 00:05:58,308
Oh.

95
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:00,666
But listen, I got to get going.

96
00:06:00,708 --> 00:06:02,124
I got a meeting with Tarantino.

97
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:03,333
And yeah, I’m gonna be late.

98
00:06:03,375 --> 00:06:05,583
Can we meet tomorrow,
talk about this a little more?

99
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:06,749
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

100
00:06:06,791 --> 00:06:09,375
Great! How’s 3pm at
the Ponti’s? You know it?

101
00:06:09,791 --> 00:06:10,624
Yeah, yeah.

102
00:06:10,666 --> 00:06:13,333
In the meantime, check out
my website. It’s on the card there.

103
00:06:13,708 --> 00:06:15,625
Okay, yeah. I will do. Thank you so much.

104
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,208
Alright. See you tomorrow.

105
00:06:19,072 --> 00:06:22,960
[indistinct chatter]

106
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,124
He said my directing style...

107
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:26,833
was masterful!

108
00:06:27,208 --> 00:06:28,875
Masterful?

109
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:31,916
And he wants me to be a
part of his upcoming project!

110
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:34,541
OMG bestfriend!

111
00:06:35,125 --> 00:06:37,958
“Pia Wurtzbach” is in tears.

112
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,208
As in!

113
00:06:40,291 --> 00:06:43,541
The Miss Universe of your life is sobbing!

114
00:06:43,708 --> 00:06:45,708
I told you bestfriend,

115
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:47,875
if something’s meant for you,

116
00:06:48,041 --> 00:06:51,541
destiny will find a way to make it happen.

117
00:06:51,583 --> 00:06:55,416
And besides, you really
belong there in America.

118
00:06:55,458 --> 00:06:58,416
Even if your Caucasian father
doesn’t want to recognize you,

119
00:06:58,458 --> 00:07:02,708
no one can deny that you’re
a true-blooded American!

120
00:07:03,208 --> 00:07:05,583
Can we please not talk
about unnecessary people?

121
00:07:06,041 --> 00:07:07,624
You’re ruining the moment.

122
00:07:07,666 --> 00:07:09,833
Sorry, bestfriend.

123
00:07:09,875 --> 00:07:11,459
My apologies.

124
00:07:11,499 --> 00:07:12,376
[playful music]

125
00:07:12,416 --> 00:07:15,291
If I were you, I won’t
let that opportunity pass.

126
00:07:15,583 --> 00:07:19,041
Give it your best shot!

127
00:07:19,083 --> 00:07:20,208
I’m not sure bestfriend.

128
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:22,833
What? Why hesitate?

129
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:26,749
People in Hollywood are chasing after you!

130
00:07:26,791 --> 00:07:29,166
Not everyone gets an offer from Hollywood!

131
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:31,749
I know. But everything’s expensive here.

132
00:07:31,791 --> 00:07:34,083
The motel where I’m staying at, it's...

133
00:07:34,125 --> 00:07:35,791
150 dollars a night.

134
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,208
That’s 7,500 pesos.

135
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,083
A night!

136
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,291
I can’t afford to stay
here that much longer.

137
00:07:41,333 --> 00:07:43,124
I’ll run out of money.

138
00:07:43,166 --> 00:07:48,416
Why ask for an advance payment
from that Hollywood Executive?

139
00:07:48,666 --> 00:07:50,041
Ask for his help.

140
00:07:50,083 --> 00:07:51,625
I’m not sure.

141
00:07:51,916 --> 00:07:53,166
I don’t think so.

142
00:07:54,416 --> 00:07:55,749
It’s embarrassing.

143
00:07:55,791 --> 00:07:58,041
But you should find a way, bestfriend.

144
00:07:58,083 --> 00:08:02,624
You’re an award-winning
filmmaker for God’s sake!

145
00:08:02,666 --> 00:08:05,499
If I were the one with the
Hollywood offer, I’d do anything,

146
00:08:05,541 --> 00:08:08,583
even if that means borrowing
money from relatives!

147
00:08:12,256 --> 00:08:16,256
[door opens]

148
00:08:49,141 --> 00:08:53,141
[shower running]

149
00:08:54,238 --> 00:08:58,238
[tiping]

150
00:09:27,708 --> 00:09:28,333
Hello?

151
00:09:28,375 --> 00:09:30,333
Hi. Uh, I saw your post online.

152
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:31,874
You’re looking for a roommate, right?

153
00:09:31,916 --> 00:09:33,374
Yeah, um...

154
00:09:33,416 --> 00:09:35,249
it’s 12 month minimum.

155
00:09:35,291 --> 00:09:36,541
I only accept cash.

156
00:09:36,583 --> 00:09:38,583
Oh, but I only need a place for two weeks.

157
00:09:38,833 --> 00:09:40,458
I thought you said you saw the ad?

158
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,083
I did.

159
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:43,249
Okay, well, it says a 12 month minimum.

160
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:45,499
I get that but the thing is

161
00:09:45,541 --> 00:09:47,624
I’m just staying here for a few days.

162
00:09:47,666 --> 00:09:49,833
After that, I'm flying
back to the Philippines.

163
00:09:51,583 --> 00:09:53,041
You’re from the Philippines?

164
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:54,100
Yeah.

165
00:09:54,333 --> 00:09:57,374
Ah… We can do 750 for two weeks.

166
00:09:57,416 --> 00:09:58,916
You’re kidding, right?

167
00:09:58,958 --> 00:09:59,958
What the fuck?

168
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,875
I don’t have time for prank callers.

169
00:10:03,125 --> 00:10:04,499
No, I’m not a prank caller.

170
00:10:04,541 --> 00:10:07,499
Look, you advertised the
room for a thousand dollars.

171
00:10:07,541 --> 00:10:11,124
So I thought, two weeks, that would be 500.

172
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:12,291
Makes sense, right?

173
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:14,708
I don’t have time for this.
It’s two in the morning.

174
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:15,708
I have to go to sleep.

175
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:16,791
Oh wait. No, no.

176
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:19,291
The thing is I only have 400 dollars.

177
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:22,291
Which means you can’t afford the room,

178
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:24,166
which means I can’t accommodate you.

179
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:25,166
Please.

180
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:28,458
I just need a temporary place to stay
while doing this project in Hollywood.

181
00:10:28,541 --> 00:10:30,083
You’re doing a Hollywood project?

182
00:10:30,125 --> 00:10:31,833
Yeah, that’s why I’m extending my stay.

183
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:33,333
Are they gonna pay you?

184
00:10:33,375 --> 00:10:36,541
Yeah, but compensation
comes after the work is done.

185
00:10:36,583 --> 00:10:37,833
Are you sure about that?

186
00:10:37,875 --> 00:10:38,749
100 percent.

187
00:10:38,791 --> 00:10:42,083
Okay, we can do 650 for the two weeks.

188
00:10:42,125 --> 00:10:43,166
It’s final offer.

189
00:10:43,208 --> 00:10:45,041
But I told you I only have 400...

190
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:45,958
Take it or leave it.

191
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,583
Okay. I’ll take it.

192
00:10:47,625 --> 00:10:48,249
Okay.

193
00:10:48,291 --> 00:10:50,958
We can meet at a coffee shop near my place.

194
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,499
You have to show me that you have the money

195
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:54,083
or I’m not letting you into my apartment.

196
00:10:54,125 --> 00:10:54,833
Okay, uh...

197
00:10:54,875 --> 00:10:56,291
what’s the location of the coffee shop?

198
00:10:56,333 --> 00:10:58,291
I'll text you more info tomorrow.

199
00:10:58,375 --> 00:11:00,166
Okay, but you are sure
you're gonna be there, right?

200
00:11:00,208 --> 00:11:01,999
Because once I leave my motel,

201
00:11:02,041 --> 00:11:03,375
I’m not gonna have anywhere else to go.

202
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,666
If you have the money,

203
00:11:04,708 --> 00:11:05,875
you have nothing to worry about.

204
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,583
Okay, but what if I were to…

205
00:11:08,833 --> 00:11:09,708
Hello?

206
00:11:12,916 --> 00:11:14,750
Well, see you tomorrow.

207
00:11:18,001 --> 00:11:22,001
[street noise]

208
00:11:29,750 --> 00:11:31,208
Oh, shit.

209
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:36,208
Wait, hey!

210
00:11:36,333 --> 00:11:37,250
Shit.

211
00:11:44,541 --> 00:11:45,708
You look tired.

212
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,708
We should get some drinks.

213
00:11:50,541 --> 00:11:51,333
Oh, uh...

214
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,208
I'm... I’m actually good.

215
00:11:53,916 --> 00:11:55,458
How about something to eat?

216
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:02,916
I actually ate just before I got here.

217
00:12:04,291 --> 00:12:05,249
Andre,

218
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:08,333
you’re gonna have to get
familiar with how we do things here.

219
00:12:08,375 --> 00:12:09,583
This is Hollywood.

220
00:12:09,625 --> 00:12:12,458
All of our meetings involve food and drink.

221
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:16,374
Well, in that case, um,

222
00:12:16,416 --> 00:12:17,791
I’ll have what you’re having.

223
00:12:18,041 --> 00:12:18,916
Good boy.

224
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:20,208
Waiter!

225
00:12:23,625 --> 00:12:25,291
Hi. What can I get you today?

226
00:12:25,541 --> 00:12:28,083
We’ll have whatever
the chef is recommending

227
00:12:28,125 --> 00:12:30,166
and a bottle of the Claret please.

228
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:31,624
I’ll be right back for that.

229
00:12:31,666 --> 00:12:32,541
Thank you.

230
00:12:35,041 --> 00:12:37,125
So, here's the thing.

231
00:12:38,041 --> 00:12:40,875
You know how exclusive Hollywood is, right?

232
00:12:42,166 --> 00:12:45,541
And you know that not
everyone that wants to work here

233
00:12:45,583 --> 00:12:47,791
gets the chance to really work here.

234
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:50,499
A beginner like you,

235
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:52,083
you need connections.

236
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:53,458
Powerful connections.

237
00:12:53,875 --> 00:12:56,208
That's why I’m offering you this project.

238
00:12:56,791 --> 00:13:00,083
I want you to be a part
of an exclusive group.

239
00:13:00,541 --> 00:13:02,875
It's called the Hollywood Elite Club.

240
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:06,708
Now, I don't offer this to just anyone.

241
00:13:06,916 --> 00:13:10,166
I only offer this to people
I really want to work with.

242
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:14,041
And after seeing your
short, I knew right away,

243
00:13:14,083 --> 00:13:15,875
you're the guy I'm looking for.

244
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:16,999
And you're timing,

245
00:13:17,041 --> 00:13:18,250
it’s just perfect.

246
00:13:18,458 --> 00:13:21,083
Hollywood is all about
diversity these days.

247
00:13:21,291 --> 00:13:24,000
We need more people of
color like you in the industry.

248
00:13:24,166 --> 00:13:25,833
And coming straight from the Philippines,

249
00:13:25,875 --> 00:13:28,083
I believe you can offer a

250
00:13:28,125 --> 00:13:31,291
very unique artistic
and cultural perspective

251
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:32,750
that no one else could.

252
00:13:32,875 --> 00:13:34,791
You will be in demand.

253
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,833
Those Hollywood Executives?

254
00:13:36,875 --> 00:13:38,958
Yeah, they’ll be chasing you down,

255
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,083
begging you to work with them.

256
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:44,416
Within a month of joining
the Hollywood Elite Club,

257
00:13:44,625 --> 00:13:46,541
you're gonna be rubbing elbows with

258
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:48,458
Ryan Reynolds, Ryan Gosling...

259
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:49,583
Ryan Seacrest?

260
00:13:49,625 --> 00:13:50,749
Of course, Ryan Seacrest!

261
00:13:50,791 --> 00:13:51,875
All the Ryans!

262
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Alright, the biggest celebrities, producers,
directors, writers in the industry.

263
00:13:57,791 --> 00:13:59,250
No, don’t do that.

264
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:00,750
Don’t cry.

265
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,750
I haven't even dropped the bomb yet.

266
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:04,708
After you join the Hollywood Elite Club,

267
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:06,416
you’re going to have the opportunity

268
00:14:06,458 --> 00:14:10,375
to make the kind of money you
never dreamed you could make!

269
00:14:10,541 --> 00:14:14,749
So how do I join this Hollywood Elite Club?

270
